# Command Pattern Implementation for Undo/Redo Functionality

## Overview

The Command Pattern is a behavioral design pattern that encapsulates a request as an object. This allows for parameterizing clients with queues, requests, and operations, making it an ideal choice for implementing undo/redo functionality in collaborative applications like document editing.

In this document, we will develop a production-ready command pattern implementation using Java with Spring Boot, Python with FastAPI, and Go. We will also cover real-world examples from industry leaders, performance metrics, testing strategies, and guidelines for migration and refactoring.

## 1. Complete Implementations

### Java (Spring Boot)

#### Command Interface and Concrete Commands

```java
// Command.java
public interface Command {
    void execute();
    void undo();
}

// InsertTextCommand.java
public class InsertTextCommand implements Command {
    private Document document;
    private String text;
    private int position;

    public InsertTextCommand(Document document, String text, int position) {
        this.document = document;
        this.text = text;
        this.position = position;
    }

    @Override
    public void execute() {
