## Introduction

In an e-commerce platform that serves millions of users daily, middleware plays a crucial role in enhancing the request/response cycle. The Decorator pattern provides a flexible way to add functionalities, such as logging, authentication, and caching, without altering the core logic of the service. However, performance bottlenecks can arise, especially during peak traffic. This document outlines a production-ready implementation of middleware using the Decorator pattern across Java, Python, and Go, along with testing strategies, performance metrics, and migration guides.

