# Adapter Pattern for API Integration in Microservices Architecture

## Introduction

In the context of migrating a legacy financial services platform to a microservices architecture, one of the key challenges is integrating with diverse third-party payment gateways. This document provides a comprehensive guide on implementing the Adapter Pattern to facilitate smooth API integration while maintaining performance, scalability, and compliance with industry standards.

### Overview of the Adapter Pattern

The Adapter Pattern is a structural design pattern that allows incompatible interfaces to work together. In our case, it will enable the integration of various payment gateway APIs, each with different protocols and data formats, into a unified interface that the microservices can interact with seamlessly.

