## Unit of Work Pattern in High-Traffic E-commerce Platform

### Introduction

The Unit of Work (UoW) pattern is essential for managing transactions in a data management layer, especially in high-traffic environments like e-commerce platforms. This pattern helps to group multiple operations into a single transaction scope, ensuring that all operations complete successfully or none at all, thus maintaining data consistency. In this document, we explore implementing the UoW pattern in Java, Python, and Go, along with real-world examples, performance metrics, testing strategies, and migration guides.

### 1. Implementation of Unit of Work Pattern

#### 1.1 Java Implementation (Spring Boot)

```java
import org.springframework.stereotype.Repository;
import org.springframework.transaction.annotation.Transactional;

import javax.persistence.EntityManager;
import javax.persistence.PersistenceContext;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

@Repository
public class UnitOfWork {

    @PersistenceContext
    private EntityManager entityManager;

    private List<Object> entitiesToSave = new ArrayList<>();

    public void registerNew(Object entity) {
        entitiesToSave.add(entity);
    }

    public void commit() {
        for (Object entity : entitiesToSave) {
            entityManager.persist(entity);
        }
        entitiesToSave.clear();
    }

    @Transactional
    public void rollback() {
        // rollback logic can be implemented here
    }
}
```

#### 1.2 Python Implementation (FastAPI)

```python
from sqlalchemy.orm import sessionmaker
from sqlalchemy import create_engine

class UnitOfWork:
    def __init__(self, db_url):
        self.engine = create_engine(db_url)
        self.Session = sessionmaker(bind=self.engine)
        self.session = self.Session()
        self.entities_to_save = []

    def register_new(self, entity):
        self.entities_to_save.append(entity)

    def commit(self):
        try:
            for entity in self.entities_to_save:
                self.session.add(entity)
            self.session.commit()
            self.entities_to_save.clear()
        except Exception as e:
            self.session.rollback()
            raise e

    def rollback(self):
        self.session.rollback()
```

