### 2. Tracing Mechanism

#### Distributed Tracing with Correlation IDs

To implement distributed tracing, we will use **OpenTelemetry** along with **Jaeger** for tracing visualization. Each incoming request will be assigned a unique **Correlation ID** that will be propagated through all microservices involved in handling the request. This allows us to trace the request lifecycle across services.

**Implementation Steps:**
1. **Inject Correlation ID**: When a request is received at the API Gateway, generate a unique Correlation ID if it does not exist in the request headers.
2. **Propagate Correlation ID**: Pass this Correlation ID to all downstream services via HTTP headers.
3. **Trace Instrumentation**: Use OpenTelemetry SDK to instrument the microservices to capture tracing data and send it to Jaeger.

**Sample Code for Propagating Correlation ID** (Node.js Example):

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const { trace } = require('@opentelemetry/api');

const app = express();

app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const correlationId = req.headers['x-correlation-id'] || generateUniqueId();
  req.correlationId = correlationId;
  res.setHeader('X-Correlation-Id', correlationId);
  next();
});

// Middleware to instrument tracing
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const span = trace.getTracer('default').startSpan(req.path);
  span.setAttribute('correlation_id', req.correlationId);
  res.on('finish', () => {
    span.setAttribute('http.status_code', res.statusCode);
    span.end();
  });
  next();
});

// Endpoint example
app.get('/data', async (req, res) => {
  // Your logic here
});

// Start server
app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server running on port 3000');
});
```

