### Builder Pattern for Complex Object Construction

The Builder Pattern is an effective way to construct complex objects step by step. In the context of an e-commerce platform, we can use it to create `Product` objects, which may have numerous attributes and variations.

#### 1. Complete Working Code

Below are the implementations of the `Product` class and its Builder in Java, Python, and Go.

**Java Implementation:**

```java
// Product.java
import java.util.List;

public class Product {
    private String name;
    private String description;
    private double price;
    private List<String> attributes;
    private List<Double> ratings; // Alternatively, could use a more complex Rating class

    private Product(ProductBuilder builder) {
        this.name = builder.name;
        this.description = builder.description;
        this.price = builder.price;
        this.attributes = builder.attributes;
        this.ratings = builder.ratings;
    }

    public static class ProductBuilder {
        private String name;
        private String description;
        private double price;
        private List<String> attributes;
        private List<Double> ratings;

        public ProductBuilder(String name, double price) {
            if (price <= 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Price must be positive");
            this.name = name;
            this.price = price;
        }

        public ProductBuilder description(String description) {
            this.description = description;
            return this;
        }

        public ProductBuilder attributes(List<String> attributes) {
            this.attributes = attributes;
            return this;
        }

        public ProductBuilder ratings(List<Double> ratings) {
            this.ratings = ratings;
            return this;
        }

        public Product build() {
            return new Product(this);
        }
    }
}

