### 2. Mapping Strategy

We will implement a mapping strategy for converting between domain models and DTOs. This includes flattening complex domain structures and handling collections.

#### Java Mapping Strategy

```java
// Mapper.java
import java.util.List;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

public class Mapper {
    public CustomerDTO toDTO(Customer customer) {
        CustomerDTO dto = new CustomerDTO();
        dto.setId(customer.getId());
        dto.setName(customer.getName());
        dto.setEmail(customer.getEmail());
        return dto;
    }

    public ProductDTO toDTO(Product product) {
        ProductDTO dto = new ProductDTO();
        dto.setId(product.getId());
        dto.setName(product.getName());
        dto.setPrice(product.getPrice());
        return dto;
    }

    public OrderDTO toDTO(Order order) {
        OrderDTO dto = new OrderDTO();
        dto.setId(order.getId());
        dto.setCustomerId(order.getCustomerId());
        dto.setProducts(order.getProducts().stream()
                .map(this::toDTO)
                .collect(Collectors.toList()));
        dto.setShippingInfoId(order.getShippingInfoId());
        return dto;
    }

    public ShippingInfoDTO toDTO(ShippingInfo shippingInfo) {
        ShippingInfoDTO dto = new ShippingInfoDTO();
        dto.setId(shippingInfo.getId());
        dto.setAddress(shippingInfo.getAddress());
        dto.setTrackingNumber(shippingInfo.getTrackingNumber());
        return dto;
    }
}
```

