## 2. Real-World Examples

- **Netflix**: Uses optimistic locking in their metadata service to manage concurrent updates to their content catalog. By applying versioning to each record, Netflix ensures that updates do not overwrite changes made by others.
- **Amazon**: In their inventory management system, Amazon employs optimistic locking to handle updates from sellers. Each product update checks the version before committing to avoid conflicts.
- **Uber**: Their ride management system uses optimistic locking to manage ride requests, ensuring that overlapping updates from multiple drivers or customers donâ€™t lead to data inconsistencies.

