## Introduction
The Specification Pattern is a powerful design pattern that allows for the encapsulation of business rules and criteria, making them easy to combine and reuse. This is particularly useful in an enterprise e-commerce application where business rules for product filtering, promotion validation, and user access control can change frequently. In this document, we will provide a complete implementation of the Specification Pattern in multiple programming languages, real-world examples, performance analysis, anti-patterns, testing strategies, and a detailed trade-off analysis.

