### Caching Specifications

To improve performance, particularly for frequently accessed data, caching can be implemented. The results of the specification checks can be stored and reused, especially in dynamic data scenarios where the underlying product data changes infrequently.

```java
// CachingSpecification.java (Java)
public class CachingSpecification<T> implements Specification<T> {
    private final Specification<T> inner;
    private final Map<T, Boolean> cache = new HashMap<>();

    public CachingSpecification(Specification<T> inner) {
        this.inner = inner;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean isSatisfiedBy(T item) {
        return cache.computeIfAbsent(item, inner::isSatisfiedBy);
    }
}

// caching_specification.py (Python)
class CachingSpecification(Specification):
    def __init__(self, inner):
        self.inner = inner
        self.cache = {}

    def is_satisfied_by(self, item) -> bool:
        if item not in self.cache:
            self.cache[item] = self.inner.is_satisfied_by(item)
        return self.cache[item]

