## 2. Model Layer

### 2.1 Design for Model Component

#### Java Implementation

```java
public class PortfolioModel {
    private final Map<String, Investment> investments = new HashMap<>();
    private final Cache<Investment> cache;

    public PortfolioModel(Cache<Investment> cache) {
        this.cache = cache;
    }

    public Future<Investment> fetchInvestment(String id) {
        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> {
            if (cache.contains(id)) {
                return cache.get(id);
            }
            Investment investment = fetchFromDatabase(id);
            cache.put(id, investment);
            return investment;
        });
    }

    private Investment fetchFromDatabase(String id) {
        // Simulate database access
        return new Investment(id, "Stock", 100.0);
    }

    public void validateInvestment(Investment investment) throws ValidationException {
        if (investment.getAmount() < 0) {
            throw new ValidationException("Investment amount must be non-negative.");
        }
    }

    // Other business logic methods...
}
```

