## 4. Presenter Layer

### 4.1 Responsibilities of the Presenter

The Presenter will be responsible for:

- Interacting with the Model to retrieve data.
- Updating the View based on Model data.
- Handling user input and events.

#### Presenter Implementation

```javascript
class PortfolioPresenter {
    constructor(model) {
        this.model = model;
    }

    async getInvestment(id) {
        return await this.model.fetchInvestment(id);
    }

    async updateInvestment(investment) {
        this.model.validateInvestment(investment);
        // Logic to persist changes...
    }
}
```

### 4.2 Data Flow and Control

The data flow in MVP is unidirectional:

1. User interacts with the View (e.g., clicking a button).
2. The View calls the Presenter.
3. The Presenter interacts with the Model to fetch or update data.
4. The Model returns data to the Presenter.
5. The Presenter updates the View with the new data.

### 4.3 Handling Real-Time Updates

To handle real-time updates, we can utilize **WebSockets** or **Server-Sent Events (SSE)**. The Presenter subscribes to changes and updates the View whenever new data is available.

